    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Plasmid retention and functional stability over 100 generations"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Directive — Establish whether the gate survives serial passage, or only survives a single overnight."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Serial passage, 1:1000 daily, 10 days, roughly 100 generations, with and without selection. Retention by plating; function by re-assaying the eight input states at days 0, 5 and 10."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Result"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Under selection: 97 percent retention, ON/OFF 26-fold falling to 24-fold. Stable."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Without selection: 41 percent retention by day 10, and the retained population’s ON/OFF falls to 6-fold — worse than plasmid loss alone predicts, indicating enrichment for cells carrying a functionally degraded gate."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The finding that matters"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Selection-free operation does not merely lose the plasmid; it selects for broken versions of it. Any deployment outside selection needs chromosomal integration, which is out of scope here and recorded in entry 18."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
